      "side": 1,
      "message": "Error will be reported if a dependency explicitly sets the hardening to disabled.\n\nI tried to spread the flag minimally as possible in the bp files. This version it only needs it where the requirement is appear.\nIdea was that enforced would help in phase 1 to add changes only to a few places, so no need to add \"hardening: \"enabled\" or \"enforced\" to many places where anyway that will be the default value later.\n\nSo if enforced is declared then all dependency should have hardening-enforced property?\nAlso maybe declared \"enabled\" state would guarantee the hardening is on without enforcing it on the dependencies..  what do you think?",
